## What PRDs are

- Product + technical specs, one per screen, under [`.gitbook/product/prd/`](../../../.gitbook/product/prd/README.md). They are the **product source of truth** (what the app does and why). `AGENTS.md` + `.ai/cursor/rules/` remain the **code** source of truth. They answer different questions and do not override each other.
- Index, screen inventory (status legend), and conventions: [`.gitbook/product/prd/README.md`](../../../.gitbook/product/prd/README.md). Domain background: [`.gitbook/product/methodology.md`](../../../.gitbook/product/methodology.md).

## Before changing a screen or its data path

- Find the matching PRD (e.g. `splash.md`, `auth.md`, `no-access.md`, `error-network-stubs.md`, `loading-indicator.md`). If the screen has no PRD yet, the matching page may say *to be specified* — treat the user/product owner as the authority and draft the PRD before/with the change.
- Treat the PRD's **functional/non-functional requirements** as the behavior contract. If your change would contradict the PRD, or the PRD is silent/ambiguous on the behavior you need, **ask the product owner** instead of guessing; then record the answer in the PRD.

## After changing a screen or its data path (same change)

- Update the matching PRD so it stays accurate, without waiting to be reminded:
  - **Status** (✅ / 🟡 / ⬜) in the page header and in the inventory table in `README.md`.
  - **Requirements** (`FR-*` / `NFR-*`), **Experience & states**, and the **Data & entities** section (Supabase tables/columns) when they change.
  - **Technical implementation** mapping (modules, key files, MVI store, navigation keys, design-system components).
  - **Open questions & planned work** — remove what shipped; add new questions surfaced by the change.
- Keep PRD prose human-first and in **English**; describe what is visible on screen. Embed screenshots from `assets/` when behavior is visual.

## Boundaries

- Do not duplicate long Kotlin rules into PRDs; link to code instead. Do not invent product copy or behavior — propose drafts and flag them for review (as the No access "Ask manager" copy is flagged).
- Spec-driven features link their spec to the PRD; see [`general/feature-workflow.md`](../../../.gitbook/general/feature-workflow.md) and [`.ai/docs/ai-workflow.md`](../../docs/ai-workflow.md).
